      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To determine whether flexible cystoscopy with a prototype slim flexible instrument is less uncomfortable than flexible cystoscopy using a standard flexible cystoscope."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS AND METHODS",
          "content": "In all, 200 men scheduled to undergo flexible cystoscopy for the follow-up of transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder were randomized in equal groups to flexible cystoscopy using the standard instrument or using the prototype slim-scope. Each patient had 11 mL of 2% lignocaine gel instilled intraurethrally 5 min before the procedure. At the end of the procedure the patient was asked to complete a 100-mm non-graphical visual analogue scale to rate how uncomfortable the procedure was."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The slim-scope was very significantly less uncomfortable than the conventional instrument (anova P < 0.001). The ease of use and views of the bladder were similar to those obtained with the conventional cystoscope."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The slim-scope offers a significant benefit in patient comfort, with little loss of image quality or ease of use."
        }
      ]},
